<article class="env-lemma" id="0CFX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CFX">Lemma <span data-tag="0CFX">74.11.8</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(f) =$“$f$ is a universal homeomorphism” is fpqc local on the base. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This can be proved in exactly the same manner as Lemma <a href="/tag/041O" data-tag="041O">74.11.3</a>. Alternatively, one can use that a map of topological spaces is a homeomorphism if and only if it is injective, surjective, and open. Thus a universal homeomorphism is the same thing as a surjective, universally injective, and universally open morphism. See Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03MH" data-tag="03MH">67.5.5</a> and Morphisms of Spaces, Definitions <a href="/tag/03MV" data-tag="03MV">67.19.3</a>, <a href="/tag/03ME" data-tag="03ME">67.5.2</a>, <a href="/tag/03Z2" data-tag="03Z2">67.6.2</a>, <a href="/tag/05Z5" data-tag="05Z5">67.53.2</a>. Thus the lemma follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/041Q" data-tag="041Q">74.11.6</a>, <a href="/tag/041R" data-tag="041R">74.11.7</a>, and <a href="/tag/041P" data-tag="041P">74.11.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>